    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d768">

                <pb facs="0880" n="1714" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/2048</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-11T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 11, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6247. For McFadden [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 434. Replying Embassy’s 5695, November 3, 6 p.m., your 559.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d768-f1"/> Your attention is called to the official publication of
                    the capture of 250,000 horses in Italy. If there should be further need of
                    animals for Army, cannot these be employed and save exportation of ammonium
                    sulphate to Spain in exchange for mules? Is it <pb facs="0881" n="1715"
                        xml:id="pg1715"/> possible that with the conclusion of an armistice this
                    purchase of mules would not need to be consummated since we are very anxious to
                    save the ammonium sulphate? Offer them flour.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
